00:05:05.413 --> 00:05:07.080
RORY PETTY: Yeah, my
name is Rory Petty.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:09.080
I'm a PM-- a product manager--

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:10.280
on Stackdriver.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:13.370
And a lot of people aren't
familiar with the Stackdriver

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:17.090
brand name, but that's basically
the brand name that encompasses

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:19.520
the suite of monitoring,
observability,

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:22.310
and logging tools
for Google Cloud.

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:24.860
So for example,
within Stackdriver,

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:27.350
there is a tool for
monitoring, like I said,

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:30.170
logging, and then
also our APM tools,

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:32.910
which are Application
Performance Management tools.

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:36.883
So that includes things like
Debugger, Trace, Profiler,

00:05:36.883 --> 00:05:38.300
so really this
kind of whole suite

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:41.390
of tools that lets
you understand

00:05:41.390 --> 00:05:43.970
how your website or your
application is performing.

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:45.620
So I like to kind
of liken it back

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:47.160
to the dashboard in your car.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:48.618
If you're driving
down the highway,

00:05:48.618 --> 00:05:50.300
the dashboard tells
you how fast you're

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:52.460
going, if your engine's
about to overheat,

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:54.180
are you about to run out of gas.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:56.690
And so, in the same way,
the Stackdriver suite,

00:05:56.690 --> 00:05:59.780
when you have it hooked up
to your mobile application,

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:02.270
your website, your
e-commerce store, whatever,

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:04.550
it provides you those
critical insights

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:08.187
into how your service
or site is performing.

00:06:08.187 --> 00:06:10.520
MARK MIRCHANDANI: So what's
your role within the program

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:11.540
manager for Stackdriver?

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:12.740
What does that kind of entail?

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:13.907
RORY PETTY: Product manager.

00:06:13.907 --> 00:06:14.780
Maybe I misspoke.

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:18.470
So basically I work on product
for Stackdriver monitoring.

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:22.220
So I work on the
core monitoring APIs,

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:25.910
I work on query notation, which
is a new feature that we have

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:27.740
in Alpha right now,
